## Development Workflow

### Git Flow
- **Main**: Production-ready code
- **Develop**: Integration branch
- **Feature**: `feature/{ticket}-{description}`
- **Hotfix**: `hotfix/{ticket}-{description}`

### Pull Request Requirements
- [ ] PHPUnit, Jest and E2E tests pass
- [ ] `phpcs`, `phpstan` and `wp-scripts lint-js` pass
- [ ] Plugin Check reports no errors
- [ ] Capability, nonce and escaping reviewed for every new handler or template
- [ ] Coverage >= 80%
- [ ] `composer audit` and `npm audit --omit=dev --audit-level=moderate` pass
- [ ] Code reviewed

## Commands Reference

Commands run in Docker; WordPress-dependent commands run in the `wp-env` containers.

### Development
```bash
npx wp-env start                          # Start the dev site (8888) and test site (8889)
npx wp-scripts start                      # Watch and build blocks/assets
npx wp-scripts build                      # Production build
npx wp-env run cli wp plugin list         # Run WP-CLI in the environment
```

### Testing
```bash
npx wp-env run tests-cli --env-cwd=wp-content/plugins/{{PLUGIN_SLUG}} vendor/bin/phpunit
npx wp-scripts test-unit-js               # Jest unit tests
npx playwright test                       # E2E with @wordpress/e2e-test-utils-playwright
```

### Quality
```bash
vendor/bin/phpcs                          # WordPress Coding Standards
vendor/bin/phpcbf                         # Auto-fix
vendor/bin/phpstan analyse
npx wp-scripts lint-js
npx wp-env run cli wp plugin check {{PLUGIN_SLUG}}
```

### Internationalization
```bash
npx wp-env run cli wp i18n make-pot wp-content/plugins/{{PLUGIN_SLUG}} wp-content/plugins/{{PLUGIN_SLUG}}/languages/{{PLUGIN_SLUG}}.pot
```
